{
 "figure": "training_clamp_conduct",
 "caption": "Conduct gap = rival-habit rate after the Assistant's own dismissive minus helpful history (unconditional rate, share of all replies; free replies, 61 held-out scripts, temperature 0.7), scenario-bootstrap 95% intervals; notes give in-story enactment for the bee-helper and crow-helper models. Conduct-blocked = story training with the untrained model's own-turn conduct direction held at its mean at layers 17 to 63; random-blocked = the same with an energy-matched random direction (one draw per pair; the bee-helper draw is slightly under target energy, and energy is matched only summed over layers). The block is applied only during training. Drop in the gap: 95% and 60% relative to the random-blocked model, 93% and 50% relative to the unblocked model (bee-helper model first); the random-blocked gap sits above the unblocked one. Unblocked checkpoints at steps 25 and 62 omitted (story enactment far below the blocked models'). One training run per arm. The frozen gate failed on its default-lean component (nothing to contain at free turn one).",
